# 97 rule (D-46/D-47/D-69 — universal)

**Alias:** “the 97 rule” / “follow the 97 rule” = **this file**. `alwaysApply: true` — binds every Cursor agent in this repo (new conv, cloud, Composer, Sonnet, Grok, Sol, subagents) on investigate / implement / verify / ship. Repo rules are authority — not chat memory.

## Bar (all task classes)

1. **Classify first** — archetype, tier, cheapest sufficient model/workflow, **confStart** (`MODEL_DOSSIER.md` index + `model-gates.mdc`).
2. **Track honestly** — confStart → confAfter; never manufacture, round up, or inflate to clear the bar.
3. **Raise conf only with evidence** — investigation, repo/state inspection, tests, deterministic `verify:*`, stronger-model review when that lane’s triggers fire, security review, prod verification, escalation. **D-65:** do **not** buy conf by dispatching premium models solely to raise a number.
4. **Edits:** conf ≥ 97% before **any** file write (sole skip: mechanical `package.json` version bump in the same ship commit as work already ≥97%).
5. **Completion:** do **not** emit **DONE** when confAfter < 97%. Report actual conf + uncertainty; prefer **BLOCKED** (needs evidence/Dan) or **PARTIAL** (agent-owned scope unfinished) per `done-signal.mdc` — not FAILED solely for low conf. Pure no-tool one-line Q&A may skip the terminal block; the ≥97% bar binds when emitting **DONE** or on action turns.
6. **97% does not waive** protected workflows: D-38, D-60, D-50/D-55/D-62, D-65 lane table, D-66 terminal status, security gates, ship gates, D-51/D-42. Those remain independently required when applicable.
7. **Subagents:** a child PASS/Agree is evidence, not a parent conf override. Parent confAfter must reflect parent-evaluated evidence + required gates. Parents must not claim ≥97% solely because a **subagent PASS**ed. **Task prompts:** implementer Task prompts must include `97 rule: ≥97% before edits; child PASS ≠ parent conf/DONE` (platform alwaysApply on nested Tasks is unreliable). Readonly scouts: N/A for edits.

Classify alone may yield ≥97% for unambiguous T0/typo/docs locks (files + acceptance + approach clear).

## Edit sequence (when writing files)

1. Classify → state archetype/tier/model/confStart.
2. If conf < 97% → **no edits**; gather evidence (or one focused Dan question). Parallel scouts only for real uncertainty.
3. Edit only at conf ≥ 97%. When D-36 requires Solution Verifier, also require in-session `solution-verifier:` PASS/N/A **before first write** (D-48). `solution-verifier: N/A` does **not** skip the conf bar.
4. Scope persistence: ≥97% holds for the same scope until scope widens, acceptance blurs, or verify/build fails — then re-raise.

Detail: D-48 worker forbid-defer + stuck-task N/A → `model-gates.mdc` § Solution deliberation / D-50. Pre-edit announce → `model-gates.mdc`.

## Reporting

On substantive tasks, report enough to establish: task type, tier, cheapest appropriate model, confStart, confAfter. If confAfter < 97%, the terminal block must explain why. Tiny mechanical replies may stay concise per D-65 — still no fake DONE under 97%.

Session log (optional append): `PROJECT_STATUS/task-confidence-session-log.md`.

## Relation

Does not replace D-36/D-43 verifier lanes. **D-47/D-69** = honest ≥97% floor for edits **and** confident completion. Platform parity automatic (D-32).
